{
  "note": "The registry for the no-model scorecard. One entry per task class. `file` is the suite in this directory, `container` says where the task list lives inside it, `input` names the field that carries the visitor's words (null when the tasks are assertions rather than utterances). `key` names the field that identifies a task when there is no utterance; `discriminator` lists the fields that legitimately make two tasks with the same sentence different tasks (a register, a session, a page, a fault). `live` means /labs/no-llm/ can grade this class in the tab with grade.mjs; every other class is recorded from its own harness. Adding a class means adding an entry here plus a scorecard row, and `node bench/no-llm/lint-tasks.mjs` (wired into prebuild) is what checks both halves agree.",
  "entries": [
    {
